fact WorkItem(id: "WI-558", description: some(value: "Proof-verification pass (the \"prove-pass gate\" deferred by WI-538): actually CHECK recorded proofs instead of recording them Pending-and-unverified. WI-538 delivered in-body 'by derivation' discharge INLINE in the typer (prove_from_gamma over Gamma + KB, typing.rs ~3593) and explicitly deferred the rest -- the comment at typing.rs:3599-3603 says an external proof's conclusion may be assumed only once the \"Gamma-snapshot + prove-pass gate\" verifies it (follow-on); until then it stays conservatively undischarged, never a silent drop. Today the loader (load.rs ~11293-11505) records EVERY proof (by derivation, by z3, structured/031, hints) as a ProofRecord fact with result Pending and a placeholder witness TrustedAxiom(\"pending -- not yet discharged\"), and NOTHING ever verifies it (grep prove_pass/verify_proof = zero). Two consequences: (1) TOP-LEVEL proofs (proof length by derivation, proof push_pop by derivation) are never checked at all -- WI-538's inline Tier-A fires only for IN-BODY proof statements, not top-level rule companions; (2) Tier-B strategies (by z3 / using / external) are no-ops (typer returns discharged=false). SCOPE: a post-typing/load pass that walks Pending ProofRecord facts and verifies each, updating result Pending -> Discharged | Failed with a REAL witness (SLD trace for derivation, external result for Tier-B) -- never silently Discharged on failure (loud + conservative). by-derivation: discharge via the SLD resolver over the proof's context (scope/inherited/definition rules, plus the Gamma-snapshot where the proof is in-body -- WI-538 names \"Gamma-snapshot + prove-pass gate\" together, so carrying the local Gamma at the proof point into the pass is part of this). Tier-B: dispatch to the external tool/driver (anthill-cli already has top-level proof-dispatch scaffolding to reuse). A Discharged conclusion may then be assumed into Gamma (the deferred half of WI-538's in-body modification rule) and discharge its obligation. RELATIONSHIP: foundation for WI-539 Part 2 (proof <op>.<clause> contract proofs, e.g. push.ensures) -- Part 2 adds the <op>.<clause> target classifier + contract-clause-to-goal extraction + body-symbolic-execution to BUILD the contract-proof Gamma, then hands goal+Gamma to THIS pass for discharge; it also completes WI-538's deferred Tier-B half. DISTINCT FROM proposal 050's self-hosted endgame gate (tabled/bottom-up holds(fact,point) evaluator), which is deferred-by-design and NOT needed here -- this is a Rust-side verification driver over the existing SLD resolver + external dispatch. Depends on WI-538 (in-body proof + Tier-A, delivered) and WI-537 (Gamma substrate, delivered)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-538"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-25T06:15:10Z"))

